-- title:
--   Retraction onto the lower-level chart ring from a q-expansion reading
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ne 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and assume that every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ which becomes $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ lies in $H$; assume $jq\mathrm{ModC}\,\mathbb{Q}$, the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot\sum$ (the integral $j$-numerator), lies in the $q$-expansion function field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\top$, i.e. the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by integral $q$-expansion ratios of modular forms of equal weight. For a subgroup $\Gamma$, $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ denotes the subalgebra of elements of $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\Gamma$ integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$ over the coefficient ring `R p`; write $\mathcal{O}_M$ and $\mathcal{O}_N$ for these rings at the levels `ΓM M H` and `ΓN p M H hpM`. Given an `R p`-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathcal{O}_N \to \mathcal{O}_M$ which is the identity on underlying Laurent series, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a ring map $\rho : \mathrm{R}\,p \to A$ lifting the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, suppose $\theta_0 : \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa((q))$ is a ring map which (i) sends the image of $c \in \mathrm{R}\,p$ to the constant series $\overline{\rho(c)}$, (ii) whenever $y \in A((q))$ has coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ equal to the $q$-expansion of $c$, satisfies $\theta_0(c) = \bar{y}$ (coefficientwise reduction), and (iii) takes values in $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{\Gamma N}\,p\,M\,H\,\mathrm{hpM})$. Then, with $\kappa$ an `R p`-algebra through $\overline{\rho}$, there are $\kappa$-algebra maps $\sigma_0 : \kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p} \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p} \mathcal{O}_N$ and $\Phi_0 : \kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p} \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa((q))$ with $\Phi_0(x \otimes c) = x\,\theta_0(c)$, such that $\sigma_0$ retracts $\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \iota_0$, is surjective, and has $\ker \sigma_0 = \ker \Phi_0$, this kernel being a minimal prime of $\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}\,p} \mathcal{O}_M$.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of Igusa's description of one branch of the mod-$p$ fibre of the modular curve of level $H$ at a level exactly divisible by $p$: reading $q$-expansions modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ cuts out a minimal prime of the special fibre whose quotient is the chart ring at the level prime to $p$, split by the degeneracy map $\iota_0$. It feeds the paired statement [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_pair_and_retraction_pair_chartAlgFin_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_pair_and_retraction_pair_chartAlgFin_gammaH), and through it the analysis of the two components of the bad fibre.
